      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "66e44c60bdd998bb2464e6ac",
      "mergedPostDetails": "While the action menu is open on your right hand, the \"GestureRightWeight\" parameter will no longer update (same for the left hand and \"GestureLeftWeight\"). When the action menu is closed, both GestureWeights work as normal; likewise, when the right side action menu is open, \"GestureLeftWeight\" works as normal and vis versa.\n\nExample: If you have a firearm shooting animation that requires you to pull the controller's right trigger to activate (thus setting \"GestureRightWeight\" to 1.00), it will not fire while the right side action menu is open. The parameter remains locked to a float value of 0.00.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "\"GestureWeight\" parameters no longer update while the action menu is open",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "66cf43ff222e72ba0aa98163",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Ive observed this too since the release of the update that fixed movement being broken while the menu was open as a side effect of the steamvr 2.0 input update https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/unable-to-move-when-radial-menu-is-open",
